title: The Republic Cannot Pay
subtitle: The debt has grown beyond what the treasury can carry.
tags: event
view-if: debt >= 32 and debt_crisis_timer <= 0 and not finale and not game_ending
priority: 3
new-page: true
face-image: img/ev_trade.svg
on-arrival: debt_crisis_timer = 8

= The Republic Cannot Pay

The Republic owes [+ debt_txt +], and this year's interest alone would empty the treasury. The Banking Clan offers to roll the debt over, on terms. The Core Moderates want cuts instead.

- @austerity: Cut spending across the Republic.
- @bailout: Accept the Banking Clan's terms.

@austerity
subtitle: The debt shrinks; the Rim and faith in the Republic pay for it.
on-arrival: debt -= 6; rim_hardship += 5; faith -= 3; mod_relation += 4; rimward_dissent += 6

Relief convoys are cancelled, patrols grounded, pensions frozen. The books balance. The Rim goes hungry.

@bailout
subtitle: The debt is rolled over; the banks gain the whip hand, and someone in the shadows profits.
on-arrival: debt -= 4; banking_dereg = 1; grand_plan += 3; guild_relation += 5; corruption += 2

The Banking Clan restructures the Republic's debts. Months later, Caucus investigators find that the new bonds were underwritten by a shell company last seen in the accounts of Damask Holdings.
